{
  "id": "roots.sub-super",
  "slug": "sub-super",
  "ladder": "vocab",
  "course": "roots",
  "unit": "where-when",
  "title": "Under and Over: sub-, super-, hypo- and hyper-",
  "short": "sub- and hypo- mean under; super- and hyper- mean over or beyond.",
  "trouble": "sub- changes shape before some letters: suc-, sup-, sur-, sus- (succumb, suppress, surreptitious, sustain). sur- can also come from super- (surplus, surfeit).",
  "prereqs": [
    "roots.pre-post"
  ],
  "xp": 1,
  "viz": [
    "vo-roots",
    "vo-word"
  ],
  "figureArchetype": "WaveFigure",
  "practice": null,
  "lesson": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "Think of a <i>submarine</i>, which goes under the sea, and a <i>superhero</i>, who rises above everyone. <b>sub-</b> means “under” and <b>super-</b> means “over” or “above.” Greek has a matching pair: <b>hypo-</b> (under, as in a <i>hypodermic</i> needle that goes under the skin) and <b>hyper-</b> (over, too much, as in <i>hyperactive</i>)."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-scene",
        "opts": {
          "scene": {
            "bg": "sea",
            "props": [
              {
                "kind": "plane",
                "x": 72,
                "y": 58,
                "s": 1.4
              }
            ],
            "animals": [
              {
                "kind": "whale",
                "x": 46,
                "y": 4,
                "s": 1.5,
                "pose": "swim"
              }
            ],
            "labels": [
              {
                "text": "SUPER: over",
                "on": "p0",
                "at": "body",
                "x": 34,
                "y": 70
              },
              {
                "text": "SUB: under",
                "on": "a0",
                "at": "body",
                "x": 84,
                "y": 30
              },
              {
                "text": "OVER AND UNDER",
                "x": 50,
                "y": 92
              }
            ],
            "alt": "A plane flies over the sea while a whale swims under the waves."
          }
        },
        "cap": "A plane flies over the sea while a whale swims under the waves."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>sub-</b> and <b>hypo-</b> = <b>under, below</b> (<i>sub-</i> also means secretly). <b>super-</b> and <b>hyper-</b> = <b>over, above, beyond</b> (<i>hyper-</i> often means too much)."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "<b>sub-</b> changes its last letter to match the root: <b>suc-</b> (<i>succumb</i>), <b>sup-</b> (<i>suppress</i>), <b>sur-</b> (<i>surreptitious</i>), <b>sus-</b> (<i>sustain</i>). The “secretly” sense comes from doing things from underneath, out of sight: <i>surreptitious</i> means snatched secretly."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "root": "sub",
          "words": [
            "subside",
            "subsequent",
            "submit",
            "succumb",
            "suppress",
            "surreptitious",
            "subterfuge",
            "sustain",
            "subvert",
            "subjective"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "Words on the list built on sub- and its shapes."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "super",
            "hyper",
            "hypo"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "super-, hyper- (over) and hypo- (under)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>subside</b><br>to become less strong; to sink lower",
            "<b>sub-</b> <i>under, down</i> + sid <i>settle, sit</i><br>→ “settle down”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>suppress</b><br>to put down by force; to keep from being seen",
            "<b>sup-</b> <i>under</i> + press<br>→ “press under”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>surreptitious</b><br>done secretly to avoid notice",
            "<b>sur-</b> <i>secretly</i> + rept <i>snatched</i> + -itious<br>→ “snatched secretly”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>subterfuge</b><br>trickery used to hide or escape something",
            "<b>subter</b> <i>beneath, secretly</i> + fug <i>flee</i><br>→ “escaping secretly”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>superficial</b><br>on the surface only; shallow",
            "<b>super</b> <i>above</i> + fic <i>face, surface</i> + -ial<br>→ “on the surface”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>superfluous</b><br>more than is needed",
            "<b>super</b> <i>over</i> + flu <i>flow</i> + -ous<br>→ “overflowing”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>supercilious</b><br>scornfully superior; looking down one’s nose",
            "<b>super</b> <i>above</i> + cili <i>eyelid</i> + -ous<br>→ “with raised eyebrows”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>hyperbole</b><br>deliberate exaggeration for effect",
            "<b>hyper</b> <i>beyond</i> + bol <i>throw</i> + -e<br>→ “a throwing beyond (going too far)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>hypothesis</b><br>a proposed explanation to be tested",
            "<b>hypo</b> <i>under</i> + thesis <i>placing</i><br>→ “a placing under (an idea to build on)”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Use the parts",
        "q": "After the party, the hall was full of <b>superfluous</b> chairs that no one needed. What does <i>superfluous</i> mean?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>super</b> (over) + <b>flu</b> (flow, as in <i>fluid</i>) + <b>-ous</b> (full of).",
          "Literally: “overflowing,” more than the container holds.",
          "The sentence fits: chairs no one needed."
        ],
        "a": "More than is needed."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Meet the word",
        "card": true
      },
      {
