        "cap": "A word from the list: superfluous.",
        "card": true
      },
      {
        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "Missing <b>sub-</b> when it changes shape. <i>suc-</i>, <i>sup-</i>, <i>sur-</i> and <i>sus-</i> are all <i>sub-</i> in disguise (<i>succumb</i>, <i>suppress</i>, <i>surreptitious</i>, <i>sustain</i>). But not every <i>sur-</i> is <i>sub-</i>: in <b>surplus</b> and <b>surfeit</b>, <i>sur-</i> comes from French and means “over,” like <i>super-</i>."
      },
      {
        "t": "note",
        "html": "A word with a story: <b>supercilious</b> comes from the Latin for eyebrow (<i>super</i>, above + <i>cilium</i>, eyelid). Picture someone raising one eyebrow and looking down on you: that is a supercilious look."
      },
